; pattern-budget: the dry-run queries cycle 0 under the frame path's own
; fixed scratch (PatternTrack.SCRATCH_BYTES, 1 MiB), so a pattern whose
; dry-run cycle out-allocates that budget is a LOAD diagnostic — never a
; silent every-frame runtime omission ("compiles clean" implies "plays at
; cycle 0"). FBA exhaustion is deterministic, so acceptance stays a pure
; function of the document. Pins the stricter acceptance (plans/elegance/04)
; with its code + budget message across native == wasm.
(transport :bpm 120)
(track :target radius :pattern (fast 8000 (pure 1)))
